# Hypothesis B patch — second crude non-vacuity proof for goal-gate-lint-spurious-warning
#
# Strategy: Fix B (rule-side stub). Extend _check_goal_gate_has_retry in
# validation.py to also recognize edge-based retry: a goal_gate node that has
# at least one outgoing edge with loop_restart=True counts as having a retry
# mechanism, and the WARNING is suppressed.
#
# This is the OPPOSITE operation from hypothesis.patch:
#   hypothesis.patch  — removes goal_gate=true from the EXAMPLE FILE (.dot)
#   hypothesis_b.patch — adds edge-inspection logic to the LINT RULE (validation.py)
#
# Different in every dimension:
#   - Different file:      validation.py  vs  examples/pipelines/00-convergence-loop.dot
#   - Different operation: adds code to the rule  vs  removes an attribute from the example
#   - Different internal path: inspects graph.outgoing_edges() for loop_restart=True
#                              vs simply not having the triggering attribute present
#   - Different fix polarity: makes the rule RECOGNIZE the existing graph topology
#                             vs making the graph NOT trigger the rule
#
# This is still deliberately crude — it is NOT a correct fix. A correct Fix B
# would also handle fallback_retry_target parity, add a comment explaining the
# edge-based retry semantics, and update the fix hint text. This patch does none
# of that; it only adds the minimal predicate needed to silence the WARNING.
#
# Verified at SHA 7a2991a88e1407cd250a840fefe9718f4d1253df:
#   - Without patch: DEFINITION.verify.sh exits 1, red_signal present in output.
#   - With patch:    DEFINITION.verify.sh exits 0, 117 tests pass.
